# Olmedo et al., TOPLAS 2018, Example 4.9 (p. 4:20): a fair coin chooses between diverging and
# tossing two fair coins (0 is heads) observed to show at least one head.  The probability that
# the last toss is heads is 2/7 under cwp, 6/7 under cwlp (wlp/wlp(1), where the diverging half
# counts as establishing the event) and 2/3 under r2.
# Expected: valid (cwlp is 6/7 >= 0.85).  The reduction is the dual, an upper bound on a least
# fixpoint: wp_(1-q)(S, 1 - [y = 0]) <= 1 - q for q = 0.85, and
# 1/2 * (1/4 + (1 - q)/4) = 0.14375 <= 0.15; it holds exactly when q <= 6/7.
nat x;
nat y;
{
	while (true) {
		skip;
	}
}[1/2]{
	{
		x := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		x := 1;
	}
	{
		y := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		y := 1;
	}
	observe(x = 0 || y = 0);
}
?Ex [[y = 0]] >= 0.85 cwlp
